msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:107
msgid "and have it inject the signed JWT in the configured header."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:110
msgid "Issuer (iss)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:111
msgid "Expected token issuer."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:113
msgid "Issuer is required."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:116
msgid "Audience (aud)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:117
msgid "Expected audience -- must identify this firewall."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:119
msgid "Audience is required."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:122
msgid "Trusted proxy IPs/CIDRs"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:123
msgid ""
"Comma separated source IPs or CIDRs of the proxy allowed to present the JWT "
"header. REQUIRED: the header is ignored from any other source (otherwise "
"anyone could forge it). The check uses the direct TCP peer (REMOTE_ADDR), "
"never a forwardable header -- so list the IP that actually connects to the "
"firewall. If another reverse proxy sits in front of the WebGUI, this must be "
"that proxy IP, and that proxy must strip the JWT header from untrusted "
"clients."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:131
msgid "At least one trusted proxy IP/CIDR is required."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:134
msgid "JWT header"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:135
msgid ""
"Request header carrying the token (e.g. X-Auth-Request-Jwt or Authorization)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:140
msgid "JWKS URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:141
msgid "HTTPS JWKS endpoint of the signer (preferred, supports key rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:144
msgid "JWKS URL must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:147
msgid "Static public key (PEM)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:148
msgid ""
"Alternative to JWKS: the signer PEM public key. The first algorithm below "
"must match it."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:152
msgid "Algorithms"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:153
msgid ""
"Comma separated, asymmetric only (RS256/ES256/PS256...). Symmetric HS* is "
"rejected."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:158
msgid "Clock skew tolerance (s)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:159
msgid ""
"Allowed clock difference (seconds) when checking exp/nbf. Default 60, max "
"300."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:163
msgid "Clock skew must be a number of seconds (0-300)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:166
msgid "Maximum token age (s)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:167
msgid ""
"Refuse a token whose \"iat\" is older than this, whatever its \"exp\" says. "
"Bounds how long a captured token stays usable when the signer issues long-"
"lived tokens. 0 disables the check."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:173
msgid "Maximum token age must be a number of seconds (0 = disabled)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:176
msgid "Single-use tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:177
msgid ""
"Accept each token only once (replay protection, keyed on \"jti\" when the "
"signer sets one). Enable when the proxy mints a fresh token per login. Leave "
"off if it reuses one token for the whole session -- the second login would "
"be refused."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:183
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:263
msgid "Username claim"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:184
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:264
msgid "Claim mapped to the local username, e.g. preferred_username or email."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:189
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:269
msgid "Groups claim"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:190
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:270
msgid ""
"Claim listing the user's groups/roles (array, or comma/space separated). Dot "
"notation reaches a nested claim, which is where most IdPs actually put them "
"- e.g. \"realm_access.roles\" or \"resource_access.<client-id>.roles\" on "
"Keycloak. A claim whose own name contains dots is matched whole first."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:199
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:279
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:284
msgid "Maximum session lifetime (s)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:200
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:280
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:285
msgid ""
"End the WebGUI session this long after login whatever the user is doing, "
"unlike the idle timeout. Enforced by the scheduled \"os-sso: expire SSO "
"sessions\" job (added for you under System > Settings > Cron) and on every "
"SSO login. 0 keeps sessions until they idle out."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:207
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:287
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:292
msgid "Maximum session lifetime must be a number of seconds (0 = disabled)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:210
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:302
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:307
msgid "Automatic user creation"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:211
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:303
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:308
msgid ""
"Discouraged on a firewall. Persists new users to config.xml with no local "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:215
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:307
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:312
msgid "Required groups"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:216
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:308
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:313
msgid ""
"Access gate: comma separated IdP group names, at least one of which the user "
"must hold to log in through this provider (WebGUI, Captive Portal and VPN "
"alike). Evaluated on the IdP-asserted groups, before any local account is "
"matched, created or updated. Leave empty to let every account the IdP "
"authenticates log in."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:223
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:315
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:320
msgid "Deprovision on refused login"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:224
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:316
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:321
msgid ""
"When a login is refused by the required groups above, also disable the local "
"account it belongs to and end its open sessions. This is how a revocation at "
"the IdP reaches the firewall: a login attempt is the only moment we hear "
"about it. Only os-sso-managed accounts are touched, never a privileged one, "
"and they are disabled, not deleted. Needs a required-groups list to be of "
"any use."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:232
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:324
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:329
msgid "Default groups"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:233
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:325
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:330
msgid "Comma separated OPNsense groups granted to mapped users."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:237
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:329
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:334
msgid "Group mapping"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:238
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:330
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:335
msgid ""
"Optional explicit IdP-group to OPNsense-group map, comma separated as "
"\"idpGroup:opnsenseGroup\". Mapped groups are trusted and may target "
"privileged groups (e.g. admins). Unmapped IdP groups fall back to a 1:1 name "
"match that refuses privileged groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:245
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:337
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:342
msgid "Strict group sync"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:246
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:338
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:343
msgid ""
"Reconcile group membership on every login: remove the user from groups os-"
"sso previously granted but the IdP no longer asserts. Only groups os-sso "
"itself granted are touched (manual assignments are kept), and the last "
"member of a privileged group is never removed. Off = additive (memberships "
"are only ever added)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:254
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:346
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:351
msgid "Enable SCIM provisioning"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:255
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:347
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:352
msgid ""
"Let this IdP push account lifecycle to the firewall over SCIM 2.0, instead "
"of os-sso only learning about changes when someone logs in. Base URL to "
"register at the IdP: <code>https://{opnsense}/api/sso/scim</code>. Accounts "
"are created disabled-free, never privileged, and a SCIM delete deactivates "
"rather than removes."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:262
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:354
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:359
msgid "SCIM bearer token"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:263
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:355
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:360
msgid ""
"Shared secret the IdP presents as \"Authorization: Bearer ...\". It is the "
"whole authentication of a write API into the account database - generate a "
"long random value and treat it as a credential."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:268
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:360
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:365
msgid "The SCIM token should be at least 32 characters."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:271
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:363
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:368
msgid "SCIM source IPs/CIDRs"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:272
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:364
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:369
msgid ""
"Comma separated addresses the IdP connects from. REQUIRED when SCIM is "
"enabled: it bounds who can even attempt to use the token, and an empty list "
"refuses every request rather than accepting any source. Matched on the "
"direct TCP peer, never on a forwardable header."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:279
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:371
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:376
msgid "Login button label"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:280
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:372
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:377
msgid "Text shown on the login-page button (defaults to the server name)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:284
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:386
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:391
msgid "Default landing URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:285
msgid ""
"Same-site relative path where users land after login (e.g. /ui/dashboard). "
"Leave empty for the requested page or the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoJwt.php:289
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:392
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:397
msgid "Landing URL must be a same-site path starting with \"/\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:63
msgid "OpenID Connect"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:119
msgid "Set the redirect/callback URL at the IdP to"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:123
msgid "Issuer URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:124
msgid ""
"OIDC issuer base URL (the part before /.well-known/openid-configuration)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:127
msgid "Issuer must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:130
msgid "Client ID"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:132
msgid "Client ID is required."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:135
msgid "Client Secret"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:136
msgid ""
"Secret of the confidential client created at the IdP. Public clients are not "
"supported. Leave empty only when the client authentication method below is "
"private_key_jwt or one of the mutual-TLS ones, which carry no shared secret; "
"a method that does need one refuses the login at run time if it is missing."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:143
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:144
msgid "Comma separated. \"openid\" is required."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:149
msgid "Use PKCE (S256)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:150
msgid ""
"Proof Key for Code Exchange. Recommended; keep enabled unless the IdP does "
"not support it."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:155
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:226
msgid "Maximum authentication age (s)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:156
msgid ""
"Send max_age so the IdP re-authenticates anyone whose session there is older "
"than this, and refuse the login if the returned auth_time says otherwise. 0 "
"disables it (the IdP session is then accepted whatever its age)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:162
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:234
msgid "Maximum authentication age must be a number of seconds (0 = disabled)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:165
msgid "Use form_post response mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:166
msgid ""
"Ask the IdP to POST the authorization response instead of putting the code "
"in the callback URL, keeping it out of browser history, Referer headers and "
"proxy logs. Enable only if the IdP supports response_mode=form_post."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:172
msgid "Pushed authorization requests (PAR)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:173
msgid ""
"Send the authorization request to the IdP over the back channel and put only "
"an opaque reference in the browser URL (RFC 9126). Nothing in between - "
"browser history, a Referer, a proxy log - then sees the scopes, the state or "
"the PKCE challenge, and none of them can be altered on the way. Needs an IdP "
"that publishes a pushed_authorization_request_endpoint; it is used "
"automatically, whatever this box says, when the IdP declares it requires PAR."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:182
msgid "Required authentication context (acr)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:183
msgid ""
"Comma separated authentication context class references, in preference order "
"- typically the one your IdP uses for MFA. They are sent as acr_values AND "
"the \"acr\" claim that comes back must be one of them. Both halves matter: "
"requesting a context is voluntary per the spec, so an IdP is free to ignore "
"it and return an ordinary session - only the returned acr proves anything. "
"Empty accepts whatever context the IdP used."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:192
msgid "Extra authorization parameters"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:193
msgid ""
"Optional \"key=value\" pairs, comma separated, appended to the authorization "
"request (e.g. \"prompt=login, ui_locales=fr\"). Parameters that carry the "
"security of the flow (state, nonce, redirect_uri, PKCE, max_age, "
"acr_values...) are ignored here - use the dedicated fields, which also "
"verify what comes back."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:200
msgid "Client authentication method"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:201
msgid ""
"How this firewall proves it is the client when it calls the token endpoint. "
"\"auto\" picks client_secret_basic or client_secret_post from the IdP "
"discovery document. The others must be set explicitly, because they need key "
"material registered at the IdP first: client_secret_jwt (the secret signs a "
"short-lived assertion and never travels), private_key_jwt (no shared secret "
"at all - see the private key below), tls_client_auth and "
"self_signed_tls_client_auth (the client certificate on the TLS handshake is "
"the credential)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:212
msgid "Client authentication method must be \"auto\" or one of: "
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:216
msgid "Assertion signing algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:217
msgid ""
"Algorithm signing the client assertion. private_key_jwt: RS256, RS384, "
"RS512, PS256, ES256 or ES384, matching the private key type. "
"client_secret_jwt: HS256, HS384 or HS512. Ignored by the other methods."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:224
msgid "Client private key (PEM)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:225
msgid ""
"Private key signing the assertion for private_key_jwt. Register its public "
"half at the IdP - either paste it there, or point the IdP JWKS URL at "
"<code>https://{opnsense}/api/sso/oidc/jwks?provider={name}</code>, which "
"serves the public key derived from this one (never the private part)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:232
msgid "Client key ID (kid)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:233
msgid ""
"Optional. Goes in the assertion header so an IdP holding several of our "
"public keys knows which one to verify with - which is what makes a key "
"rollover possible without an outage."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:239
msgid "Mutual-TLS client certificate (PEM)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:240
msgid ""
"Certificate presented to the token endpoint for tls_client_auth or "
"self_signed_tls_client_auth. RFC 8705: when the IdP publishes "
"mtls_endpoint_aliases, the aliased token endpoint is used automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:246
msgid "Mutual-TLS private key (PEM)"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:247
msgid "Private key of the certificate above."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:251
msgid "Follow Entra ID group overage"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:252
msgid ""
"Entra ID stops sending the groups claim once a user is in more than about "
"200 groups, replacing it with a pointer to Microsoft Graph. Enable this to "
"follow that pointer, otherwise the most heavily grouped users - usually the "
"administrators - arrive with no groups at all. The firewall asks Graph on "
"its own behalf, so the app registration needs the APPLICATION permission "
"GroupMember.Read.All (or Directory.Read.All) with admin consent. Graph "
"answers with group object ids, the same values the ordinary claim carries, "
"so write the group map against ids either way. Only Microsoft Graph hosts "
"are ever called."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:290
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:295
msgid "Applies to"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:291
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:296
msgid ""
"Where this provider may be used, comma separated: \"webgui\", \"portal\" "
"(captive portal), \"vpn\". Empty means all three, which is what it was "
"before this setting existed. It matters because every provider otherwise "
"puts a button on the firewall login page: a provider added for guest wifi, "
"or for the VPN, is also a WebGUI door - and one left without required groups "
"because the portal zone does its own group check then admits the whole "
"directory to the WebGUI."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:299
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:304
msgid "Applies to accepts only: "
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:376
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:381
msgid "Base URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:377
msgid ""
"Public base URL of this firewall (https://host[:port]) used to build the "
"OIDC redirect/callback URL registered at the IdP (and the post-logout URL). "
"Required: without it the URL is derived from the request Host header, which "
"the client controls. Set it to exactly what the IdP has registered (mind a "
"reverse proxy or port-forward)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:383
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:388
msgid "Base URL is required and must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoOidc.php:387
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:392
msgid ""
"Same-site relative path where users land after a successful WebGUI login "
"when no specific page was requested (e.g. /ui/dashboard or /index.php). "
"Leave empty to use the originally requested page, or the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:61
msgid "SAML 2.0"
msgstr ""

#. Every SP endpoint carries ?provider=<server name>: each SAML server is its
#. own SP identity, so two IdPs never share an EntityID/ACS.
#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:121
msgid "SP ACS URL is"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:122
msgid "metadata at"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:123
msgid "({name} = this server's name; the live URLs are shown under Base URL)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:126
msgid "IdP metadata URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:127
msgid ""
"Optional https URL of the IdP SAML metadata document. When set, the "
"EntityID, SSO/SLO endpoints and signing certificate below may be left empty "
"and are read from it (cached 24h) -- which also means an IdP signing-key "
"rotation is picked up on its own. Anything you fill in by hand wins over the "
"document."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:133
msgid "Metadata URL must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:136
msgid "IdP EntityID"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:137
msgid "Required unless an IdP metadata URL is set above."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:141
msgid "IdP SSO URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:142
msgid ""
"IdP Single Sign-On endpoint (HTTP-Redirect binding). Required unless an IdP "
"metadata URL is set."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:146
msgid "SSO URL must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:149
msgid "IdP SLO URL"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:150
msgid ""
"IdP Single Logout endpoint (HTTP-Redirect). Leave empty to disable SLO; "
"defaults to the SSO URL on Keycloak."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:153
msgid "SLO URL must be a valid https URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:156
msgid "IdP x509 certificate"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:157
msgid ""
"PEM certificate (or the bare base64 body) of the IdP signing cert, NOT a "
"fingerprint. Required unless an IdP metadata URL is set; pinning one here "
"also stops the metadata document from rotating it."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:165
msgid "SP certificate"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:166
msgid ""
"Optional PEM certificate for the SP (only if the IdP requires signed "
"requests)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:170
msgid "SP private key"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:171
msgid "Optional PEM private key matching the SP certificate."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:175
msgid "NameID format"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:176
msgid ""
"Requested NameID format. \"persistent\" suits most setups; some IdPs need "
"\"unspecified\" or \"emailAddress\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:181
msgid "Username attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:182
msgid ""
"Assertion attribute mapped to the local username. Leave empty to try "
"\"uid\", \"username\", \"preferred_username\" and then fall back to the "
"NameID. Set it when the IdP emits OID-style names (e.g. "
"urn:oid:0.9.2342.19200300.100.1.1) or its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:188
msgid "Email attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:189
msgid ""
"Assertion attribute carrying the email. Empty tries \"email\" then \"mail\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:193
msgid "Display name attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:194
msgid ""
"Assertion attribute carrying the full name. Empty tries \"displayName\", "
"\"cn\" then \"name\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:199
msgid "Groups attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:200
msgid "SAML assertion attribute carrying the user's groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:205
msgid "Require signed response"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:206
msgid ""
"Require the SAML Response (message) itself to be signed, not only the "
"assertion. Enable when the IdP supports it (mitigates signature-wrapping)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:210
msgid "Accept SHA-1 signatures"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:211
msgid ""
"Legacy escape hatch. By default an assertion signed - or digested - with "
"SHA-1 (or MD5, or RIPEMD-160) is refused: the certificate may be the right "
"one, but a signature over a broken hash proves the IdP signed some document, "
"not this one. Tick this only for an IdP that cannot be reconfigured for RSA-"
"SHA256 yet, and untick it once it can."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:219
msgid "Force re-authentication"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:220
msgid ""
"Send ForceAuthn, asking the IdP to authenticate the user again instead of "
"silently reusing its existing session. Combine with the maximum "
"authentication age below, which checks the IdP actually did: ForceAuthn is "
"only a request."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:227
msgid ""
"Refuse the login when the assertion says the user authenticated at the IdP "
"longer ago than this (its AuthnInstant). The SAML counterpart of the OIDC "
"max_age check. An assertion with no AuthnInstant is refused rather than "
"trusted. 0 disables it (any session age is accepted)."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:237
msgid "Required authentication context"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:238
msgid ""
"Comma separated AuthnContextClassRef values, typically the one your IdP uses "
"for MFA (e.g. urn:oasis:names:tc:SAML:2.0:ac:classes:MultiFactor or an IdP "
"specific one). They are sent as a RequestedAuthnContext AND the "
"AuthnContextClassRef that comes back must be one of them - both halves "
"matter, because honouring the request is voluntary, so only the answer "
"proves anything. An assertion carrying no context at all is refused rather "
"than trusted. Empty accepts whatever context the IdP used. The SAML "
"counterpart of the OIDC acr check."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:248
msgid "Sign the AuthnRequest"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:249
msgid ""
"Sign the login request we send, and declare it in the SP metadata. Needs the "
"SP certificate and private key below. Required by some IdPs (ADFS in a "
"strict configuration, Keycloak with \"Client signature required\"); harmless "
"otherwise, since the IdP learns our signing certificate from the same "
"metadata."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:256
msgid "Send AuthnRequest by HTTP-POST"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:257
msgid ""
"Deliver the login request in a self-submitting form instead of a redirect. "
"Enable when the IdP only accepts the HTTP-POST binding, and point the IdP "
"SSO URL above at its POST endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:263
msgid "Allow IdP-initiated login"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:264
msgid ""
"Accept an assertion that answers no request of ours (the \"launch from the "
"IdP dashboard\" flow), posted to this server's own ACS URL. Off by default "
"and worth keeping off: an unsolicited assertion carries no proof the browser "
"receiving it asked to log in, so anyone who can obtain one can silently sign "
"a visitor in as that account. Signature, audience, expiry and single-use "
"replay checks all still apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:272
msgid "Require encrypted assertions"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:273
msgid ""
"Require the IdP to encrypt the assertion to the SP certificate. Needs an SP "
"certificate and private key above, and the IdP configured to encrypt. "
"Decryption works whenever the SP key is set; this makes an unencrypted "
"assertion a failure."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:279
msgid "Require encrypted NameID"
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:280
msgid "Same, for the NameID element alone."
msgstr ""

#: src/opnsense/mvc/app/library/OPNsense/Auth/SsoSaml.php:382
msgid ""
"Public base URL of this firewall (https://host[:port]) used to build the SP "
"EntityID, ACS, SLO and metadata URLs. Required: without it those URLs are "
"derived from the request Host header, which the client controls. Set it to "
"the public URL the IdP reaches (mind a reverse proxy or port-forward) so the "
"signed Destination/ACS match."
msgstr ""

